  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64689,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 324,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "<p>Mature cystic teratoma of the cervix mostly occurs in adult women and presents as cervical masses or polyps. Yolk sac tumour (YST) associated with somatic carcinoma typically occurs in perimenopausal and postmenopausal women {27631522}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-29T16:20:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64690,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 324,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Germ cell tumours arising in the cervix are rare.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:15:33"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64691,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 324,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:15:33"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64692,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 324,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "<p>Proposed origins of mature cystic teratoma include aberrantly migrated germ cells {7444199}, uterine pluripotent stem cells {21979590}, and residual fetal tissue after incomplete abortion. A subset of cervical YSTs in younger/premenopausal patients are probably true germ cell neoplasms, but for YSTs in perimenopausal/postmenopausal patients, pluripotent somatic stem cell origin or retrodifferentiation of somatic carcinoma has been proposed because of the frequent association with somatic carcinomas {27631522}. Reports of choriocarcinoma associated with clear cell carcinoma and adenocarcinoma NOS support both the non-gestational and possible somatic origin of choriocarcinoma in some cases.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-29T16:20:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64693,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 324,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:15:33"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64694,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 324,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "<p>The histological features of teratoma {12713570; 7668946}, YST {22293272}, and non-gestational choriocarcinoma {28118159; 28830246} of the cervix are similar to those of their ovarian counterparts, and metastasis from ovary must be excluded.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-29T16:20:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
